 :org/member-count-basis "source-pinned (Colombia only): 62,553 Juntas de Acción Comunal plus 1,500 Asociaciones de Juntas grouped into 35 Federaciones, with at least 6,300,000 affiliated people per the Ministerio del Interior — described as the largest organized civil structure in Colombia. Chilean juntas de vecinos and the other countries listed are NOT included in these figures."
 :org/legal-registration :registered
 :org/governance-model :democratic
 :org/mission-statement "Elected neighborhood boards with legal standing to contract public works, mediate disputes and channel municipal funds."
 :org/refresh-checked "2026-07-26"
 :org/refresh-result "Re-checked and the precise figure was KEPT over a divergent official one. The Unidad para las Víctimas (a Colombian state agency) publishes approximately 70,000 JAC, approximately 10 million affiliates and approximately 1,300 asociaciones, undated and stated as approximations; the Ministerio del Interior figures recorded here are 62,553 / 6,300,000 / 1,500 and are precise. Two state sources disagree by roughly 12 percent on bodies and 60 percent on people, and neither dates its count. The corpus keeps the precise, attributable figure and records the disagreement rather than averaging them."
 :org/source-name "Ministerio del Interior de Colombia figures, via Wikipedia (Juntas de Acción Comunal)"
 :org/source-url "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juntas_de_Acci%C3%B3n_Comunal"
 :org/source-date "2024"
 :org/source-tier :secondary
 :org/source-caveat "Secondary; the datos.gov.co JAC president registry (2022-2026) would give a directly countable primary figure."
 :org/pinned-on "2026-07-25"
 :org/data-provenance "source-pinned"
 :source/dataset "community-coverage"}

